**Two blocking defects**, both contradicting a property the tool claims about itself:

- **R1 — genuine fail-open.** `regular_file` catches only `FileNotFoundError` from `lstat`. Any other `OSError` escapes the `except ContractError` handler at `:314` that unlinks the output, so `assemble` leaves an **unverified** `assembled.md` on disk with no receipt and exit 1. Demonstrated by chmod-000 inside the real post-write window. The other 5 of 6 window mutations fail closed correctly with precise diagnoses.
- **R2 — terminator smuggling.** The guard `any(line == terminator for line in text.splitlines())` catches only prefixes that are Python line-splitting boundaries. A separator-class matrix showed space/tab/NBSP/any non-separator prefix smuggles a second `BODY-END` into the output; a `.strip()`-tolerant consumer then truncates at line 8 instead of line 12. Same root cause lets a body forge the assembler's own `sha256=` provenance line.

Seven further corrections: `write_exclusive` OSError (R3), `path` is the only unvalidated manifest string and a NUL makes a section report "not yet produced" forever (R4), "canonical JSON" claimed but duplicate keys accepted (R5), `prompt_sha256` is decorative — echoed, never verified (R6), `lstat`→`read` TOCTOU won **1 in 1,861,153** attempts (R7), immutability and `lane.sh` integration overclaims — the tool is wired to nothing (R8), doc minors (R9).

